# ─── Line endings are LF, in the repository AND in every working tree ────────
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS NOT COSMETIC.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default. Without a `.gitattributes` it
# stores LF in the object database and hands the working tree CRLF, so the file
# on disk is not the file that was committed. For most of this repo that is
# merely untidy. For `contracts/` it breaks reproducibility outright:
#
#   solc hashes the EXACT SOURCE BYTES into the `metadata` field of its output,
#   and that metadata is appended to the deployed bytecode.
#
# So the same commit of `DuelEscrow.sol` compiles to different bytecode on a
# Windows checkout than on a Linux one. Measured, not assumed: the file was
# 25,459 bytes with 514 CRLF on disk against 24,945 bytes with 514 LF in git —
# a 514-byte difference, exactly the carriage returns. That is enough to make
# `contracts/out/DuelEscrow.json` fail to match a fresh compile on a clean
# Windows clone, and enough to make BaseScan's source verification fail against
# a contract that is byte-for-byte the reviewed one.
#
# `contracts/build.ts` also normalises to LF before it hands source to solc,
# and both belong here: that normalisation makes the compiler's answer
# host-independent even in a checkout predating this file, and this file fixes
# the cause, so the bytes on disk are the bytes that were committed and
# reviewed. Neither makes the other redundant.
*                   text=auto eol=lf

# Named explicitly rather than left to `text=auto`'s content sniffing, because
# these are the ones where a stray CR changes a hash rather than a diff.
*.sol               text eol=lf
*.ts                text eol=lf
*.tsx               text eol=lf
*.json              text eol=lf
*.md                text eol=lf
*.css               text eol=lf
*.html              text eol=lf
*.toml              text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF whatever the host: a CR at the end of a shebang line
# is a "bad interpreter" error, not a whitespace difference.
*.sh                text eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.gif               binary
*.zip               binary
